{
  "_comment": [
    "WAVE-AN-NAMES-1. Does a plan entry's move turn accelerated networking on",
    "for the primary network interface, and on which row of the wave settings",
    "is the machine named? ONE answer, decided once: the engine works it out",
    "from the plan entry (Get-VmfPlannedAnOutcome, PowerShell) and records it",
    "on the entry as acceleratedNetworkingOutcome (plan-entry v20). The pages",
    "read the record (VmfHelp.anOutcomeRow in src/dashboard/help.js) and never",
    "work it out again.",
    "recorded: true - the engine is held to 'outcome' for 'entry', and the",
    "pages, given the entry with that record, to 'row'.",
    "recorded: false - an entry the engine gives no record: one that does not",
    "move (Get-VmfPlannedAnOutcome gives null; outcome null). The planner and",
    "every writer record every entry that moves, so the pages read no setting",
    "in place of the record: no record is none (OLD-VERSION-READERS-REMOVE-6).",
    "row: on (Machines that get accelerated networking turned on), decides",
    "(Machines where the move decides accelerated networking), none.",
    "Held by tests/unit/WaveAnNames.Tests.ps1 and tests/js/wave-an-names.test.js."
  ],
